DTSTART:20260805T193000Z
DTEND:20260805T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260805T000000Z
SUMMARY:Teen Art Club @ South Regional Library
DESCRIPTION:For creatives in grades 6-12:\n\nJoin us for casual creativity 
 sessions with other artists at the South Regional Library! Meetings will 
 have an easy-to-learn art project planned (and coloring sheets at the 
 ready)\, but feel free to bring your sketchbook or current creative 
 project! You also have the option to do an art project of your own choosing 
 instead\, with the materials from our Teen Art Cart: put together a 
 collage\, fold origami\, make a zine...there's all sorts of possibilities! 
 \n\nThe Teen Art Club meets on the first and third Wednesdays of each month 
 in the Children's Programming Room\, to the left of the Teen Space 
 😄\n\nRegistration not required but appreciated!\n\nFeel free to reach 
 out to Ezra\, Senior Teen Librarian and club facilitator\, with any 
 questions at eletson@dconc.gov.\n\n \n
LOCATION:South Regional - Children's Programming Room\, South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="Ezra L.":MAILTO:eletson@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Social
UID:LibCal-14288-17079036
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17079036
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260805T200000Z
DTEND:20260805T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260805T000000Z
SUMMARY:3D Printing Orientation Part 1 (virtual)
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to 3D print from idea to design to fabrication! In 
 this two part orientation series\, you will learn how to design and 3D 
 print your own ideas.\n\nNote: You must sign up and attend both orientation 
 parts to gain 3D printer access. If you have take one (but not both) of the 
 orientations\, you can register for this set and only attend the 
 orientation part you are missing.\n\nIf you are under the age of 13 you 
 must have a parent or guardian present to sign up for 3D Printer OS to send 
 prints to the library.\n\n \n\n3D Printing Orientation Part 1: 3D Design - 
 Wednesday\, August 5th\, 4-5pm\n\n\n	Learn about the basics of 3D printing 
 and how to create your own design.\n\n\n3D Printing Orientation Part 2: 
 Printing Designs - Wednesday\,  August 12th\, 4-5pm\n\n\n	Learn about our 
 specific 3D printers and the software you use to send a print.\n\n\n 
 \n\nRegistration required. Sessions are held virtually over Zoom.
LOCATION:Virtual
ORGANIZER;CN="Kyle Lampart":MAILTO:klampart@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:3D Printing, Maker, STEAM, Virtual
UID:LibCal-14288-17140728
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17140728
END:VEVENT
