SUMMARY:Stuffed Animal Sleepover (Drop Off)
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wondered what happens in the library when it’s 
 closed?! Drop off your stuffie/lovie for a Stuffed Animal Sleepover at the 
 library for a super fun adventure! Participants and their stuffed animal 
 friends are invited to join us for a storytime and craft on Thursday 
 afternoon. We'll tuck our friends into bed...but something tells us they 
 may get up to some mischief when the librarians go home! \n\nThen\, pick up 
 your friend Friday\, August 7th from 10-11 am and enjoy a special breakfast 
 treat. This event is open to children ages 2-9\, and registration is 
 required. Space is limited to 50 stuffed animals. \n\n(Please note that 
 this is a sleepover for stuffed animals - no humans allowed!) \n\n 
 \n\nQuestions? Please call (919) 560-8595 or email Kristen at 
 kstockdale@dconc.gov
LOCATION:Southwest Meeting Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Kristen Stockdale":MAILTO:kstockdale@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Story Time, Summer Reading
