SUMMARY:Book Babies
DESCRIPTION:Please join us on Fridays at 9:45 a.m. for special bonding time 
 with your little one (ages 0-24 months)! At this lapsit-style storytime\, 
 we will spend about 20 minutes engaging in structured learning through 
 bounces\, rhymes\, songs\, and books\, followed by 15-45 minutes of 
 unstructured play and socialization time.\n\nNote: A television is used 
 during the first part of the program to display the words to the songs and 
 rhymes (to support adult engagement)\; there are no moving pictures. \n\nTo 
 celebrate 2026 Summer Reading and its theme\, "Unearth a Story\," we will 
 be focusing on dinosaurs from June 12 - August 7\, 2026.\n\nAll are 
 welcome! If you have any accessibility questions or accommodation needs\, 
 please contact Chelsea at cromero@dconc.gov. We ask that all requests be 
 made at least three (3) business days prior to the event to ensure we can 
 provide the best accommodations possible!\n
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Chelsea Romero":MAILTO:cromero@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Story Time
UID:LibCal-14288-16508940
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16508940
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260807T140000Z
DTEND:20260807T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20260807T000000Z
SUMMARY:Stuffed Animal Sleepover (Pick up)
DESCRIPTION:Please stop into the Children's Program Room anytime between 
 10-11 am to pick up your stuffed animal from their night at the library and 
 enjoy a breakfast treat! \n\n \n\nHave you ever wondered what happens in 
 the library when it’s closed?! Drop off your stuffie/lovie for a Stuffed 
 Animal Sleepover at the library for a super fun adventure! Participants and 
 their stuffed animal friends are invited to join us for a storytime and 
 craft on Thursday afternoon. We'll tuck our friends into bed...but 
 something tells us they may get up to some mischief when the librarians go 
 home! \n\nThen\, pick up your friend Friday\, August 7th from 10-11 am and 
 enjoy a special breakfast treat. This event is open to children ages 2-9\, 
 and registration is required. Space is limited to 50 stuffed animals. 
 \n\n(Please note that this is a sleepover for stuffed animals - no humans 
 allowed!) \n\n \n\nQuestions? Please call (919) 560-8595 or email Kristen 
 at kstockdale@dconc.gov
LOCATION:Southwest Regional - Children's Programming Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Kristen Stockdale":MAILTO:kstockdale@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Summer Reading
