SUMMARY:Intermediate Spanish Book Club
DESCRIPTION:Join us at our new Intermediate Spanish Book Club! We offer a 
 welcoming space for readers at the A2/B1 Spanish level who want to improve 
 their language skills through engaging literature and conversation. Our 
 current book is "La Casa en Mango Street" by Sandra Cisneros. \n\nReading 
 and discussion schedule/Calendario de Lectura y Discusión-\n\nJuly 11: 
 Introduction and Chapters 1-10\n\nJuly 25: Chapters 11-24\n\nAugust 8: 
 Chapters 25-44\n\nWho Should Join?\n\n· Learners reading at an A2-B1 
 level.\n\n· Adults interested in improving Spanish through 
 literature.\n\n· Anyone who enjoys thoughtful discussion in a supportive 
 environment.\n\nRegistration is required. Please register for each meeting 
 you plan to attend\n\nQuestions? Please contact Jessica at 
 jllundin@dconc.gov or group facilitator Renee Carroll at 
 renecarol33@gmail.com\n
LOCATION:Adult Programming Room\, South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="Jessica L.":MAILTO:jllundin@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club, Spanish
