SUMMARY:Drop-in Tech Support
DESCRIPTION:Drop-in for one-on-one technical support with library staff. A 
 chance to troubleshoot common device problems and learn basic computer\, 
 tablet\, or smartphone skills. This series will take place on the second 
 Wednesday of each month. \n\nWho should attend: Anyone with questions 
 about technology. People who want to improve their tech skills. Those who 
 want hands-on help or troubleshooting with their device. \n\nWhat we can 
 help with:  \n\n\n	\n	Using library e-resources (Libby\, Hoopla\, Consumer 
 Reports\, etc) \n	\n\n\n\n	\n	Setting up an email or online account 
 \n	\n\n\n\n	\n	Filling out an online form \n	\n\n\n\n	\n	Setting up your 
 device \n	\n\n\n\n	\n	Installing or using apps \n	\n\n\nWhat to bring: Your 
 device (laptop\, tablet\, or smartphone)\, chargers\, and any relevant 
 passwords. \n\nPlease note that registration is required to ensure 
 dedicated technical assistance with library staff. We cannot help with 
 resume creation. Additionally\, we cannot offer medical\, financial\, or 
 legal advice. If you need in-depth assistance with job seeking\, we can 
 refer you to the library's Business Services. \n\nFor more information\, 
 please contact Anne Wells at awells@dconc.gov
LOCATION:Southwest Regional - Children's Programming Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Anne W.":MAILTO:awells@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Digital/Tech Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-17291855
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17291855
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260812T220000Z
DTEND:20260812T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260812T000000Z
SUMMARY:Genre of the Month Book Club
DESCRIPTION:12 months\, 12 genres\, 12 chances to broaden your reading 
 horizons!\n\n \n\nWelcome to the Genre of the Month Book Club! Each month\, 
 we explore a different (sub)genre\, and you choose to read any book that 
 fits that theme--no assigned reading here! Then\, join us on the second 
 Wednesday of every month at Boxyard RTP. Grab yourself a drink or snack as 
 we discuss what we read and the genre as a whole.\n\n \n\nThe book club 
 meets outside\, so dress for the weather! Our table is located next to RTP 
 Uncorked and the elevator\, near the dog park. If you've found a table 
 reserved for book club\, you're in the right place!\n\n\n\n \n\nClick on 
 one of the months below to see what our members chose to read!\n\n 
 \n\nJanuary: Self Help\n\nFebruary: Romantasy\n\nMarch: Satire\n\nApril: 
 Poetry\n\nMay: Cozy Mystery\n\nJune: Epistolary\n\nJuly: 
 Cyberpunk\n\nAugust: Coming of Age/Bildungsroman\n\nSeptember: Banned 
 Classic \n\nOctober: Gothic Horror\n\nNovember: History\n\nDecember: Short 
 Story Collection/Anthology\n\n \n\nQuestions? Email Elle at 
 kfarmer@dconc.gov.\n\n \n\nBoxyard RTP\n\n900 Park Offices\n\nResearch 
 Triangle Park\, NC 27709\n
LOCATION:Offsite
ORGANIZER;CN="Elle F.":MAILTO:kfarmer@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club
UID:LibCal-14288-15686754
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15686754
END:VEVENT
