BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260815T140000Z
DTEND:20260815T153000Z
DTSTAMP:20260815T000000Z
SUMMARY:Durham Grown: The Durham County Library Garden Club
DESCRIPTION:Getting To Know Your Trees! General Care Throughout Your Tree's 
 Life \n\nPeople often overlook the needs of trees from young to mature. 
 When a tree is planted in our urban and suburban landscapes\, it is outside 
 of its natural habitat and needs care to maintain its beauty. Most problems 
 that occur with trees start as something small but compound over the tree's 
 life\, potentially leading to significant issues. A small adjustment now 
 could lead to major benefits down the road.  \n\nJoin Matt Archibald\, ISA 
 Board Certified Master Arborist\, to learn through a proactive\, healthcare 
 focused lens how to care for trees young and old to keep them healthy\, 
 strong\, and thriving! \n\nMatt Archibald is an ISA Board Certified Master 
 Arborist\, Tree Risk Assessment Qualified\, Prescription Pruning 
 Qualified\, and a 12-year veteran of the Arboricultural industry. He is a 
 residential consultant at Leaf & Limb but has worked with multiple 
 municipalities\, universities\, and organizations to educate people and 
 keep their trees healthy. Matt's passion comes from learning about trees 
 and nature and how we can best incorporate natural practices to keep our 
 ecosystems healthy. His favorite subjects are Tree Identification\, 
 Biology\, Biomechanics\, Ecology\, and Soil Science. \n \n\nSaturday August 
 15th starting at 10 a.m. in the auditorium at the Durham County Main 
 Library located at 300 North Roxboro Street.   \n\nParking is available in 
 the library lot or at the North Queen Street Garage which is locate at 115 
 North Queen Street which is located directly across the street from the 
 library. Parking is free in the garage. Bring your parking ticket to a 
 library service point for validation.      \n\n \n\nImage description: 
 Large old pine tree that is twisted and bent from a Japanese folding 
 screen.  \n\nImage credit: Umezawa Ryūshin\, Pine Tree\, 1914/1934\, 
 two-panel folding screen\; lacquer on paper
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Megan Koslofsky":MAILTO:mkoslofsky@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Classes & Lectures, Durham, Environmental, Gardening, Health & Fitness
UID:LibCal-14288-15882797
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15882797
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260815T140000Z
DTEND:20260815T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260815T000000Z
SUMMARY:The Homebuyer Blueprint
DESCRIPTION:Are you ready to stop renting and start building wealth through 
 homeownership? Join us for an informative and engaging homebuyer session 
 designed to walk you through the entire process—from preparing 
 financially to closing on your dream home.\n\nDuring this session\, we’ll 
 break down what it really takes to buy a home in today’s market\, how to 
 position yourself as a strong buyer\, and how working with the right team 
 can save you time\, stress\, and money. You’ll also hear directly from a 
 trusted lender about financing options\, credit insights\, and down payment 
 assistance programs.\n\nWhether you’re just starting to think about 
 buying or ready to make a move soon\, this session will give you the 
 clarity\, confidence\, and strategy you need.\n\nCome ready to learn\, ask 
 questions\, and take your next step toward homeownership.\n\nThis 
 instructional workshop is presented by Shawndria McCoy\, real estate broker 
 and founder of McCoy Homes Realty\, and Alexandria Tindall\, community 
 mortgage loan officer and assistant vice president of North State Bank.
LOCATION:Conference Room #3214\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Austin Daniels":MAILTO:ausdaniels@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Business, Finance
UID:LibCal-14288-16856893
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/calendar/14288/homebuyer
END:VEVENT
