BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260818T200000Z
DTEND:20260818T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260818T000000Z
SUMMARY:Reading Time with Ms. Chloe
DESCRIPTION:Registration Required. To schedule a time\, go to: Make an 
 Appointment - DCoL Events & Room Reservations - Durham County 
 Library\n\nDoes your child need more reading practice and could benefit 
 from more reading aloud time? Or are they just learning phonics sounds and 
 need more practice to build blending skills? Then this program is for them! 
 Schedule a 20-minute session for your child with Ms. Chloe to work together 
 with your child on reading and blending practice. You’re welcome to bring 
 your own book or I’ll pull some books that will work for their range. 
 \n\nWhile parents/ guardians don’t have to attend\, they must remain on 
 the children’s floor while their child is attending their session.\n\nFor 
 more information\, contact: chloebullock@dconc.gov
LOCATION:Main Library - Children's Area\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Chloe Bullock":MAILTO:chloebullock@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-16591880
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16591880
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260818T220000Z
DTEND:20260818T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260818T000000Z
SUMMARY:3D Printer Orientation Part 1 (In-Person)
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to 3D print from idea to design to fabrication! In 
 this two part orientation series\, you will learn how to design and 3D 
 print your own ideas.\n\nNote: You must sign up and attend both orientation 
 parts to gain 3D printer access. If you have take one (but not both) of the 
 orientations\, you can register for this set and only attend the 
 orientation part you are missing.\n\nThe in-person orientation is a great 
 choice for those who need extra support with navigating a computer. A 
 laptop will be provided.\n\n \n\n\nIf you are under the age of 13 you must 
 have a parent or guardian present to sign up for 3D Printer OS to send 
 prints to the library.\n\n \n\n \n\n3D Printing Orientation Part 1: 3D 
 Design - Tuesday\, August 18th\, 6-7:30pm\n\n\n	Learn about the basics of 
 3D printing and how to create your own design.\n\n\n3D Printing Orientation 
 Part 2: Printing Designs - Tuesday August 25th\, 6-7:30pm\n\n\n	Learn about 
 our specific 3D printers and the software you use to send a print.\n\n\n 
 \n\nRegistration required.
LOCATION:Computer Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Kyle Lampart":MAILTO:klampart@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:3D Printing, Innovation Lab, Maker, STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-17140837
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17140837
END:VEVENT
