SUMMARY:Back-to-Financial-School
DESCRIPTION:\na {\n    text-decoration: none\;\n    color: #464feb\;\n}\ntr 
 th\, tr td {\n    border: 1px solid #e6e6e6\;\n}\ntr th {\n    
 background-color: #f5f5f5\;\n}\n\n\n\nBack to Financial School is a 
 family-friendly workshop designed to help elementary students and their 
 parents build strong money habits together before the school year begins. 
 Presented by Self-Help Credit Union\, this interactive session will include 
 fun activities and hands-on learning to introduce children to 
 age‑appropriate financial concepts like saving\, spending wisely\, and 
 setting small goals. Parents will learn simple strategies for teaching 
 money skills at home and guiding kids as they make their first financial 
 choices. Join us for a playful and practical program that helps families 
 start the school year feeling confident and money-smart.
LOCATION:Main Children's Programming Room\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Austin Daniels":MAILTO:ausdaniels@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Business, Finance
