BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260902T220000Z
DTEND:20260902T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
SUMMARY:SciFi & Fantasy Book Club
DESCRIPTION:This month the SciFi & Fantasy Book Club will read R.F> Kuang's 
 acclaimed novel Babel. Copies are available in a variety of formats from 
 the library.\n\nFrom the publisher:\n\nFrom award-winning author R. F. 
 Kuang comes Babel\, a thematic response to The Secret History and a tonal 
 retort to Jonathan Strange & Mr. Norrell that grapples with student 
 revolutions\, colonial resistance\, and the use of language and translation 
 as the dominating tool of the British empire. Traduttore\, traditore: An 
 act of translation is always an act of betrayal. 1828. Robin Swift\, 
 orphaned by cholera in Canton\, is brought to London by the mysterious 
 Professor Lovell. There\, he trains for years in Latin\, Ancient Greek\, 
 and Chinese\, all in preparation for the day he'll enroll in Oxford 
 University's prestigious Royal Institute of Translation--also known as 
 Babel. Babel is the world's center for translation and\, more importantly\, 
 magic. Silver working--the art of manifesting the meaning lost in 
 translation using enchanted silver bars--has made the British unparalleled 
 in power\, as its knowledge serves the Empire's quest for colonization. For 
 Robin\, Oxford is a utopia dedicated to the pursuit of knowledge. But 
 knowledge obeys power\, and as a Chinese boy raised in Britain\, Robin 
 realizes serving Babel means betraying his motherland. As his studies 
 progress\, Robin finds himself caught between Babel and the shadowy Hermes 
 Society\, an organization dedicated to stopping imperial expansion. When 
 Britain pursues an unjust war with China over silver and opium\, Robin must 
 decide ... Can powerful institutions be changed from within\, or does 
 revolution always require violence?
LOCATION:Innovation Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Larkin Coffey":MAILTO:lcoffey@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club, Summer Reading
UID:LibCal-14288-17390457
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17390457
END:VEVENT
